    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-327720",
      "knowledge_point_id": "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Phase for the Amplitude-Phase Form for Sine",
      "problem": "Given that the expression $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the **exact** value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($ \n{{field-1}} $)$",
      "worked_solution": "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{7}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
