    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-274603",
      "knowledge_point_id": "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Amplitude-Phase Form for Sine",
      "problem": "Express $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ in the form $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,{90}^{∘}).$\n\n$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=$\n {{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘})$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\  & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={2}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+4 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =8 \\\\ R & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+{45}^{∘})\n$$",
